## Frequently Asked Questions

### What is the average bathroom renovation cost in Richmond, BC in 2026?
Based on real projects completed across Richmond — from Steveston townhouses to Sea Island condos — the typical bathroom renovation cost in Richmond ranges from $15,000 to $45,000 in 2026. A basic refresh (new vanity, toilet, and paint without tile work) runs $6,000–$12,000. A complete renovation with new tile floor and shower surround, new vanity, and updated fixtures runs $15,000–$28,000. A high-end ensuite with large-format tile, frameless glass, heated floor, and premium fixtures: $30,000–$55,000+.

### Why do bathroom renovation costs vary so much in Richmond?
Bathroom renovation costs in Richmond vary based on four primary factors: scope (cosmetic refresh versus full gut renovation), plumbing changes (keeping existing rough-in locations versus moving drains), tile (square footage, tile size, pattern complexity, and material quality), and property type (condo above a concrete slab costs 2–3x more to move drains than a wood-frame townhouse). The difference between a $15,000 and a $35,000 bathroom in Richmond is usually the tile scope and whether plumbing rough-ins are moved.

### What hidden costs should I budget for in a Richmond bathroom renovation?
Common hidden costs in Richmond bathroom renovations: (1) subfloor damage — rotted plywood under old tile is found in approximately 30% of Vancouver-area bathroom renovations and adds $500–$2,000 to repair; (2) outdated plumbing materials — pre-1990 homes in Richmond often have polybutylene or galvanized pipes that should be replaced when accessed; (3) old electrical wiring — GFCI outlets are required near water in BC, and older wiring may need upgrading; (4) mould remediation — found in approximately 20% of full bathroom gut renovations in Metro Vancouver''s humid climate; (5) permit fees — typically $500–$1,500 for Richmond bathroom permits.

### Do Richmond bathroom renovation costs differ for condos versus townhouses?
Yes significantly. Concrete-slab condos in Richmond cost 2–3x more to move bathroom drains than wood-frame townhouses because drains must be rerouted above the slab rather than through the floor assembly. A simple drain relocation that costs $1,500–$3,000 in a wood-frame townhouse costs $4,000–$9,000 in a concrete high-rise. This is why design-in-place bathroom renovations (keeping all rough-in locations) are particularly cost-effective in Richmond condo buildings, and why the first question to ask is whether plumbing needs to move.

### How do I get an accurate bathroom renovation quote in Richmond?
To get an accurate quote for a Richmond bathroom renovation: have tile, vanity, and fixture selections ready before meeting contractors (selections that are TBD get estimated as average-priced, often producing misleading quotes); specify whether you want rough-in locations kept or changed; provide accurate measurements of the bathroom including ceiling height; and ask specifically whether the quote includes permit fees, strata application assistance, and a contingency for subfloor or plumbing surprises. Quotes that do not address these items are likely to produce change orders.

### What have real Richmond bathroom renovations actually cost?
Based on real projects completed by Reno Stars across Richmond — from Steveston townhouses to Sea Island condos — completed bathroom renovations have ranged from: minimalist wall-hung vanity, frameless shower, subway tile: $15,000–$18,000 (2–3 weeks); gray tile full gut with rainfall shower and porcelain throughout: $17,000–$20,000 (4–5 weeks). See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/zh-Hant/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners. These real project data points reflect what Richmond homeowners are actually spending at the most popular renovation tiers — not theoretical ranges. The total cost is driven primarily by tile selection (large-format porcelain costs more than subway tile), shower complexity (rainfall head and niche vs standard showerhead), and vanity style (wall-hung vs freestanding vs built-in). Requesting a detailed line-item quote ensures the estimate reflects your specific Richmond bathroom''s actual scope.


