## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a new bathroom vanity cost and install in Vancouver?

Bathroom vanity supply and installation in Metro Vancouver costs $700–$7,200+ depending on size, material, and complexity. A stock single vanity (24–36 inch, big box store) supply + plumbing hook-up: $700–$1,500. A mid-range semi-custom double vanity (48–60 inch, quartz top, undermount sinks): $2,500–$4,500. A full custom vanity with integrated storage, specialty stone top, and vessel sinks: $4,000–$8,000+. Installation labour: $300–$800 for standard vanity swap (same location, existing plumbing). Moving vanity to new wall location adds $800–$2,500 for plumbing relocation. No permit needed for same-location vanity replacement.

### What is the most popular vanity style in Vancouver bathrooms in 2026?

The most popular bathroom vanity styles in Metro Vancouver for 2026: (1) **Floating (wall-mounted) vanity** — creates visual floor space, easy to clean under; standard in new Vancouver condos; (2) **Slab-front doors** (no profile) — clean, contemporary; replaces shaker front as the top request; (3) **Natural wood grain** — white oak, walnut veneer; warm counterpoint to white tile; (4) **Warm white** (vs. cool bright white) — greige, linen, or off-white cabinet finish; (5) **Double sinks in primary ensuites** — strongly requested for any primary bathroom over 60 sqft; (6) **Mixed materials** — stone or quartz top contrasting with a wood-finish lower cabinet. Grey vanities (dominant 2016–2022) are declining.

### Do I need a plumber to install a bathroom vanity in Vancouver?

Technically no — replacing a vanity in the exact same location is within a skilled DIYer''s ability (turn off shut-off valves, disconnect supply and drain, install new vanity, reconnect). However, in Metro Vancouver, a licensed plumber is required if: (1) you''re moving the drain or supply lines to a new location; (2) the building is a strata and the bylaws require licensed tradespeople for plumbing work; (3) any permit is involved. Reno Stars includes a licensed plumber for all bathroom renovation projects as part of the trade coordination — vanity replacement is typically 2–4 hours of plumbing labour ($250–$600).

### How do I choose the right vanity size for my Vancouver bathroom?

Measuring rules for Vancouver bathroom vanity sizing: allow minimum 15 inches from vanity centre-line to side wall or obstacle (21 inches preferred); allow minimum 30 inches between double sink centre-lines; leave minimum 21 inches of clear floor space in front of vanity (ADA recommends 30 inches). Common sizes and contexts: 24-inch single (small condo 客用洗手間 or ensuite); 36-inch single (standard 4-piece bathroom); 48–60-inch double (primary ensuite, recommended for couple use); 72-inch+ custom (luxury primary ensuites). See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/zh-Hant/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners. Reno Stars measures existing plumbing and floor plan constraints before recommending any vanity size.

### What countertop is best for a bathroom vanity in Vancouver?

Best bathroom vanity countertop materials for Metro Vancouver in 2026: (1) **Quartz** — top choice; non-porous, stain-resistant, no sealing required, $400–$1,200 for a 48–60 inch top with undermount sinks; (2) **Porcelain slab** — ultra-durable, large format, low maintenance; gaining market share; (3) **Cultured marble** — integrated sink option, budget-friendly ($300–$700 for a standard top), no seams, but dated look; (4) **Natural marble** — luxurious but porous; requires sealing every 1–2 years; not recommended for high-moisture bathroom use; (5) **Solid surface (Corian)** — seam-free custom shapes, repairable scratches; mid-range price. Reno Stars recommends quartz as the best balance of durability, maintenance, and aesthetics for Metro Vancouver bathrooms.

### How long does a bathroom vanity installation take in Vancouver?

A standard bathroom vanity installation in Vancouver takes 3–6 hours for an experienced plumber/carpenter team: disconnect and remove old vanity (30–60 min), install new vanity cabinet and countertop (1–2 hours), reconnect plumbing and install new faucet and drain (1.5–2 hours), caulk and seal (30 min). A floating/wall-hung vanity with in-wall plumbing modifications takes 1–2 days. If your existing rough-in plumbing is accessible and in good condition, same-day installation is routine. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Most vanity replacements in Metro Vancouver do not require a permit — they''re like-for-like replacements of fixtures on existing rough-ins.

