## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a laundry room renovation cost in Vancouver?

A laundry room renovation in Vancouver typically costs $1,800–$18,000+ depending on scope. A basic closet laundry refresh (new appliances, painted walls, shelving) runs $1,800–$4,000. A combined laundry/bathroom or full-room conversion with tiling, cabinetry, and plumbing runs $8,000–$18,000+. Projects requiring new electrical (240V outlet) or moving supply/drain lines add $2,000–$5,000. Reno Stars real-project data puts the average dedicated laundry room renovation in Metro Vancouver at $6,500–$12,000.

### What is included in a laundry room renovation?

A full laundry room renovation typically includes: washer/dryer hookup (water supply, drain, 240V electrical), flooring (LVP or tile), cabinetry and countertop for folding, wall-mounted or freestanding utility sink, lighting, ventilation for dryer exhaust, and drywall/paint. Higher-end renovations add custom cabinetry, quartz counters, steam-rated tile, and in-floor heating. Permits are required when moving plumbing or adding circuits.

### How long does a laundry room renovation take in Vancouver?

Most laundry room renovations take 5–12 business days once permits are issued (if needed). A simple refresh with no plumbing changes takes 3–5 days. A full conversion with new plumbing and electrical takes 8–12 days. Permit processing in Metro Vancouver adds 2–6 weeks to the timeline if structural or mechanical changes are involved. Reno Stars provides a week-by-week schedule at the time of contract signing.

### Is a laundry room renovation worth it in Vancouver?

Yes — a functional, well-organized laundry room adds real appraisal value and is one of the most requested features by Vancouver home buyers. Real estate agents in Metro Vancouver consistently report that a dedicated laundry room (vs. laundry in a closet or garage) adds $10,000–$25,000 in perceived value on homes in the $900K–$2M range. The practical ROI (time saved, appliance longevity, reduced water damage risk) typically justifies costs of $5,000–$15,000 within 3–5 years.

### Can I add a laundry room to my Vancouver home without major construction?

Often yes. If existing 240V electrical and water supply/drain are nearby, creating a laundry space can be done with minimal structural work — a partition wall, some plumbing stub-outs, and proper ventilation. Conversions from a hallway closet, spare bathroom, or unused utility space are common. Reno Stars assesses feasibility during the free in-home consultation. The key constraints are: distance to main drain stack, ceiling height for dryer venting, and panel capacity for a 240V circuit.

### What permits are required for a laundry room renovation in Vancouver?

Laundry room renovation permit requirements in Metro Vancouver: Plumbing permit — required when adding or relocating drain connections or supply lines. Adding a utility sink or creating a new laundry room rough-in requires a plumbing permit in all Metro Vancouver municipalities. Electrical permit — required when installing a new dedicated 240V dryer circuit or 20A washer circuit. Adding outlets or circuits to an existing panel requires a licensed electrician and permit. Mechanical permit — if adding or modifying dryer exhaust ventilation through the building envelope (exterior wall or roof). Simple laundry refreshes (paint, flooring, cabinetry on existing rough-ins) typically do not require permits. Permit fees in Metro Vancouver: $150–$400 for residential plumbing permits, $100–$300 for electrical. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping.

