3. **Request a written estimate** that breaks down trades line-by-line. A good quote should clearly separate permits, design, demo, framing, plumbing, electrical, HVAC, kitchen, bathroom, flooring and finishes. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping.
4. **Plan financing** — most homeowners use a HELOC at prime+0.5%, a refinance pulling equity, or the federal Greener Homes loan stack. See [Basement Renovation Financing in BC 2026](/zh-Hant/blog/basement-renovation-financing-bc-guide/) for current rates.
5. **Schedule the build** for spring or fall — basement work isn''t weather-sensitive, but kitchen/cabinet lead times are 4–6 weeks so order early. Our [cabinet refinishing](/en/services/cabinet/) service can transform your cabinets without full replacement.

See our [verified five-star reviews](/en/reviews/) from Metro Vancouver homeowners.

