### What upgrades add the most cost to a Vancouver bathroom renovation?

The three biggest cost drivers in a Vancouver bathroom renovation are: (1) Custom tile work — a fully tiled shower with custom patterns adds $2,000–$6,000 over a prefabricated surround. (2) Plumbing relocation — moving a drain or adding heated floors adds $1,500–$3,000 per relocated fixture. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. (3) Custom vanity cabinetry — a custom built-in vanity runs $1,500–$4,000 vs $400–$800 for a stock vanity. Combining all three luxury upgrades (curbless shower, full custom tile, custom cabinetry) is what pushes Vancouver bathroom renovations from the $18,000–$25,000 mid-range up to $35,000–$45,000+.

