### How long does a condo renovation typically take vs a house renovation in Vancouver?

Condo renovations in Vancouver typically take 20–40% longer than equivalent house renovations for the same scope. Key reasons: (1) Elevator booking — most high-rise stratas require advance booking for materials and waste removal, often 1–5 days wait per delivery. (2) Strata approval — building managers must pre-approve renovation contractors before work starts, adding 1–4 weeks of process. (3) Noise restriction hours — typical Vancouver strata bylaws restrict work to 8am–6pm weekdays, with no work on statutory holidays. A 3-week house bathroom renovation often runs 4–5 weeks in a condo with these constraints.

