## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a 3-piece bathroom renovation cost in Vancouver?
A 3-piece bathroom (toilet, sink, and either shower or tub) renovation in Metro Vancouver typically costs $12,000–$22,000 for a full renovation at mid-range finishes. A basic cosmetic refresh — new fixtures, paint, vanity replacement without moving plumbing — runs $5,000–$10,000. High-end 3-piece bathrooms with custom tile, frameless glass, and designer fixtures can reach $30,000+. The biggest cost variable is whether you keep existing plumbing locations; moving a single drain adds $2,000–$4,000.

### How much does a 4-piece bathroom renovation cost in Vancouver?
A 4-piece bathroom (toilet, sink, tub, and separate shower) renovation in Metro Vancouver ranges from $18,000–$40,000 at mid-range finishes. The separate shower is the key cost differentiator: a tiled shower with frameless glass door adds $6,000–$14,000 over a basic tub-shower combo. High-end 4-piece ensuite renovations in Vancouver — with custom cabinetry, heated floors, steam showers, and premium fixtures — routinely reach $50,000–$80,000. Our [cabinet refinishing](/en/services/cabinet/) service can transform your cabinets without full replacement.

### Is a 5-piece bathroom worth the additional cost in Vancouver?
A 5-piece bathroom (toilet, dual sinks, tub, and separate shower — the standard master ensuite layout) typically costs $28,000–$60,000+ to renovate in Metro Vancouver. The ROI depends on overall home value: in a $1.5M+ detached home, a well-executed 5-piece ensuite directly supports resale value and typically recoups 70–85% of renovation costs. In condos or townhouses, the return is more modest because buyers expect proportionate suite sizes.

### Does bathroom size or piece count drive renovation cost more in Vancouver?
Piece count affects cost more than raw square footage in most Vancouver bathroom renovations. A small 35-sqft 3-piece costs less than a small 4-piece primarily because of the trade work involved — separate drain, glass enclosure, tile for two wet areas. Square footage matters most for tile costs and labour time, but the number of plumbing fixtures and wet area walls drives the majority of what contractors quote.

### What permits are needed for a bathroom renovation in Vancouver and what do they cost?
Any bathroom renovation involving plumbing changes or electrical work requires a City of Vancouver building permit. Our [Critical Load Panel Installation](/en/services/critical-load-panel/) service upgrades your home electrical capacity for modern renovation demands. Permit fees typically run $500–$1,500 depending on scope; contractor permit application and expediting adds $300–$800. Total permit-related budget: $800–$2,300. Cosmetic work — swapping fixtures on existing rough-ins, retiling, vanity replacement — generally does not require a permit. Always confirm with your contractor before assuming no permit is needed.


### How does bathroom renovation timeline compare by piece count in Vancouver?

Vancouver bathroom renovation timelines by piece count, without layout changes: 2-piece 客用洗手間: 2–3 weeks. 3-piece bathroom: 3–5 weeks. 4-piece master bathroom: 5–7 weeks. 5-piece luxury ensuite: 7–10 weeks. Adding a layout change (moving plumbing, relocating drain): add 2–4 weeks to each. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. These timelines assume permits are obtained in advance — Metro Vancouver permit processing adds 1–4 weeks depending on municipality and permit type.


