## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much does a home renovation cost in Burnaby in 2026?

Home renovation costs in Burnaby are similar to Metro Vancouver averages. Representative 2026 project costs from Reno Stars'' Burnaby portfolio: kitchen renovation $22,000–$68,000 (average: $35,000), bathroom renovation $12,000–$48,000 (average: $24,000), [basement suite](/en/guides/basement-suite-cost-vancouver/) $65,000–$110,000, whole-house renovation $90,000–$280,000. Burnaby''s permit processing times (4–8 weeks for residential) and municipal fees are slightly faster and lower than the City of Vancouver. Materials and labour costs are equivalent across Metro Vancouver. Reno Stars has completed 40+ renovation projects in Burnaby across Metrotown, South Slope, Deer Lake, Heights, and Sullivan areas.

### How long does renovation permit processing take in Burnaby?

Burnaby''s building permit processing times for residential renovations in 2026: simple permits (single room, no structural) — 4–6 weeks; mid-complexity (bathroom addition, basement suite) — 6–10 weeks; complex or structural — 8–14 weeks. Burnaby offers online permit applications (MyBurnaby portal) which speeds up intake but not review times. Plumbing and electrical permits (ESA) are separate from the building permit and run 1–3 weeks. Older Metro Vancouver homes may also need our [Poly-B Pipe Replacement](/en/services/poly-b-replacement/) service to eliminate unsafe plastic piping. Reno Stars submits complete, well-documented permit packages to Burnaby which minimizes revision requests and accelerates approvals.

### Does Burnaby allow secondary suites in single-family homes?

Yes — Burnaby allows one secondary suite per single-family home in most RS zones. Requirements: BC Building Code fire separation (1-hour rated walls and ceiling between suite and principal dwelling), minimum 6''5" ceiling height, proper egress, separate electrical sub-panel or circuit, and a separate exterior entrance. The suite must be registered with the City of Burnaby after permit close-out. Detached garden suites (backyard cottages) are also permitted in many Burnaby zones under recent zoning changes — check the Burnaby Zoning Bylaw for your specific lot. Reno Stars has completed 15+ legal suite conversions in Burnaby.

### What neighbourhoods in Burnaby have the highest renovation ROI?

Renovation ROI in Burnaby varies by neighbourhood and housing type. Highest ROI neighbourhoods for kitchen and bathroom renovations (based on property values and buyer expectations): Metrotown condo/townhouse market ($800K–$1.5M) — renovated kitchens command $20,000–$50,000 premium; South Slope detached homes ($1.4M–$2.5M) — full renos return 60–75% on investment at sale; Heights detached ($1.2M–$2M) — strong demand for legal basement suites (ROI through rental income). Lower-value areas (some Deer Lake rental properties) have tighter margins — renovation ROI depends heavily on entry price and post-reno comparable sales.

### Do I need strata approval for a renovation in a Burnaby condo?

Yes — Burnaby strata properties (condos and townhouses) require strata council approval before renovation work begins. Requirements vary by strata corporation bylaws but typically include: written application with scope of work, contractor license number, and COI (certificate of insurance) naming the strata as additional insured ($2M–$5M CGL); designated work hours (typically weekdays 8 AM–5 PM, no weekends); use of freight elevators (booking required); floor protection in common areas. Reno Stars provides the complete strata documentation package for Burnaby condo clients — we''ve worked with over 20 different Burnaby strata corporations. See our guide to [BC Strata Renovation Rules](/zh-Hant/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) for Metro Vancouver homeowners.


