Metro Vancouver homeowners increasingly include a [heat pump HVAC upgrade](/services/heat-pump-hvac/) in their renovation plans — these systems provide efficient heating and cooling year-round, and qualify for BC Hydro and CleanBC rebate programs.


When renovation projects add new appliances, EV charging stations, or smart home systems, a [critical load panel upgrade](/services/critical-load-panel/) is often needed to safely handle the increased electrical load.


If you live in a strata property (condo or townhouse), review BC''s [strata renovation rules](/blog/strata-renovation-rules-vancouver/) before starting work — many projects require strata council approval and must follow specific noise, hour, and contractor requirements.
## Frequently Asked Questions

### How much do frameless glass shower doors cost in Vancouver?

Frameless glass shower doors in Metro Vancouver cost $1,200–$3,500 installed for a standard 34–36 inch door. A frameless glass shower enclosure (door + 1–2 glass panels) runs $2,500–$5,500 installed. Premium options with low-iron glass (ultra-clear, no green tint), custom sizing, or specialty hardware run $4,000–$8,000+. Semi-frameless (partial frame) options cost $900–$2,200. Framed aluminum-channel doors start at $600–$1,200. Most Metro Vancouver frameless shower door projects include: measurement, custom fabrication (2–3 week lead time), and installation in 2–4 hours.

### What is the difference between frameless and semi-frameless shower doors?

Frameless shower doors use thick tempered glass (3/8" or 1/2") with minimal metal hardware — no frame around the glass perimeter. Semi-frameless doors have a metal frame on two or three sides (usually the hinge side and top/bottom) but exposed glass on the visible panel edge. Full-framed (aluminum channel) doors surround all glass edges with metal. Key differences: frameless = cleanest look, easiest to clean, most expensive; semi-frameless = good balance of looks and cost; full-frame = most affordable, shows more metal, harder to clean due to channels. In Vancouver''s contemporary bathroom market, frameless outsells all others combined. For expert [Pre-Sale Renovation Advice](/en/services/realtor/) before listing, speak with our renovation team.

### How long do frameless shower doors last in Vancouver?

Properly installed frameless glass shower doors last 20–30+ years in Metro Vancouver homes. The glass itself is virtually indestructible (3/8"–1/2" tempered safety glass). What wears: rubber seals (sweep and gaskets) need replacement every 5–10 years ($100–$300); hinges and hardware (chrome, brushed nickel, matte black) last 10–20 years depending on quality; magnetic door closures last 7–15 years. Hard water in Metro Vancouver''s Lower Mainland (particularly East Van and Fraser Valley) accelerates mineral scaling on glass — daily squeegee use or a hydrophobic glass coating ($200–$400 application) dramatically extends the "like-new" appearance.

### Can I install a frameless shower door myself in Vancouver?

Not recommended. Frameless shower door installation requires: precise measurement and ordering to 1/16" tolerance (custom-fabricated; not returnable), drilling through tile and setting anchors in the wall or curb (risk of tile cracking), precise hinge alignment (1–2mm off = door won''t swing or seal), and handling 80–120 lb glass panels safely. In Metro Vancouver, a botched installation typically costs more to fix than hiring a professional initially. Reno Stars installs frameless shower doors as a standalone service and as part of bathroom renovations — typically a 2–4 hour installation by a 2-person crew.

### What glass options are available for Vancouver shower doors?

Glass options for Vancouver shower doors: (1) **Clear** — most popular; shows tile and design; easy to see water spots (but easiest to clean); (2) **Low-iron (Starphire/Optiwhite)** — crystal clear with no green tint; best for white/light grey tile; costs 15–25% more; (3) **Frosted/acid-etched** — privacy option; hides water spots between cleanings; popular for main bathrooms; (4) **Rain/textured** — wavy or rain pattern; privacy with visual interest; (5) **Bronze or grey tinted** — adds warmth or drama; less common in Metro Vancouver''s bright contemporary aesthetic. Glass thickness: 3/8" for doors under 60" tall; 1/2" recommended for taller or heavier doors.

### How do I clean and maintain frameless glass shower doors in Vancouver?

Frameless glass shower door maintenance in Vancouver: Daily squeegee — the single most effective maintenance habit. After each shower, squeegee the glass to prevent hard water mineral deposits from etching the surface. Vancouver''s water is soft (low mineral content) compared to Calgary or Toronto, making mineral buildup less aggressive. Weekly clean with a diluted white vinegar solution or a commercially available glass cleaner — avoid abrasive cleaners that scratch the coating. Monthly: inspect the hinges, handles, and hardware for early signs of corrosion; wipe dry. Regrout and reseal the perimeter seal every 3–5 years. With this routine, quality frameless glass doors in Vancouver last 15–25 years without refinishing.

